      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:c7d452ebc496121e759b859e061ccef5310d765f805dc2cbc4eddf7ff139c01b",
      "text": "Operator dashboards join sensitive telemetry to interfaces that may control a trading bot. The evidence supports restricting network exposure, checking the authority behind dashboard and data-source credentials, separating monitoring access from trading actions, redacting secrets, and auditing operator changes. Prometheus and Grafana document that dashboard presentation does not itself restrict underlying query access. Freqtrade documentation and a maintainer discussion show why remote UI access requires more than transport encryption. OWASP supplies event-field and log-protection guidance. An incident account and a malware investigation illustrate credential compromise; vendor statements remain attributed. Dashboard freshness and control separation are design inferences from these documented failure modes, not validated features of a particular deployment.",
